(4) CONSEQUENCE: sum-free families have uniformly smaller 3-body terms
    Schur triples   (n=  6): median |delta| = 0.012390
    sum-free triples(n=294): median |delta| = 0.001149
    ratio = 10.78x

  => additive structure in the speed set is what drives the k-body terms.
     'Hard family' = 'additively rich family'.  This is Schur/sum-free
     territory, and it says the extremal LRC(14) families should be the
     additively richest 13-sets -- e.g. arithmetic progressions, which is
     exactly what the corpus kept finding as the adversarial construction.
